{"abstract":"We present a Research-through-Design exploration of Machine Learning (ML) as design material in music-making. We designed Picnic, an interactive musical installation that augments everyday objects in a picnic basket into a loop-based sampler which allows users to build rhythms with a variety of percussive, harmonic and more-than-human sounds. Embracing ML’s inherent uncertainty, we intentionally used an underfitted real-time classification model to create a playful and ambiguous music-making experience with the system. Through an evaluation with 23 participants of varying musical expertise and AI interest, we found that the system’s misclassifications made participants engage in a creative dialogue, constantly adapting to its unpredictability. Furthermore, when errors occurred, participants tended to criticise themselves rather than the system, indicating a tendency to overtrust the system. Our findings contribute with insights into the potential for using ML as design material for music-making and other creative domains.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Montesinos, Lucía","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-884850"],"filters":{"added":"2026-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Machine learning","Music interaction","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"machine learning as design material for music making","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3800645.3812932","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-884850","ids":["itu-ae0dc15b-dfec-464a-bc48-97a37ecf5180"],"keyword":["Machine learning","Music interaction","Research through design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-255DDB249752FA341F3AB80FF6637899"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3800645.3812932","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucía","key":"montesinospau","last":"Montesinos","locid":"8999b149-c410-4fd7-882f-9be2e31a4fe8","name":"Montesinos, Lucía","orcid":"0009-0002-1438-6461","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3800645.3812932","eisbn":["9798400725630"],"isbn":["9798400725630"],"pages":"4768-4784","status":"p","title":"DIS '26: Proceedings of the 2026 Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105042950407"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ae0dc15b-dfec-464a-bc48-97a37ecf5180"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Machine Learning as Design Material for Music-Making","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-884850","year":"2026","yearsub":"2026"}
{"abstract":"We present Picnic, an interactive musical installation exploring Machine Learning (ML) as design material for embodied music-making. The system transforms everyday objects in a picnic basket into a loop-based sampler, allowing users to create rhythms by striking cups, plates, and cutlery. A microphone captures sounds that are classified in real-time by an ML model, triggering percussion samples, melodic layers, and bird calls that loop sequentially. Embracing ML’s inherent uncertainty, we intentionally used an underfitted classification model to create a playful and ambiguous music-making experience.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Montesinos, Lucía","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-884851"],"filters":{"added":"2026-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Interaction design","Machine learning","Music interaction","Musicking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"picnic playful music making with everyday objects and machine learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3802974.3808034","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-884851","identifier":[{"id":"105042609045","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c6b4b341-5646-4573-b007-863fc5086be4"],"keyword":["Interaction design","Machine learning","Music Interaction","Musicking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-9B6E77723B62937CF41F03D4990D4911"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3802974.3808034","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucía","key":"montesinospau","last":"Montesinos","locid":"8999b149-c410-4fd7-882f-9be2e31a4fe8","name":"Montesinos, Lucía","orcid":"0009-0002-1438-6461","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ching","key":"chiuanyenpedh","last":"Chiuan Yen","name":"Chiuan Yen, Ching","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jung-Joo","key":"leepedh","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Jung-Joo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ellen","key":"yiluendopedh","last":"Yi-Luen Do","name":"Yi-Luen Do, Ellen","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Clement","key":"zhengpedh","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Clement","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daisy","key":"yoopedh","last":"Yoo","name":"Yoo, Daisy","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tony","key":"langpedh","last":"Lang","name":"Lang, Tony","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3802974.3808034","isbn":["9798400726323"],"pages":"608-612","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"DIS '26 Companion